<i>Lentimicrobium saccharophilum</i> gen. nov., sp. nov., a strictly anaerobic bacterium representing a new family in the phylum <i>Bacteroidetes</i>, and proposal of <i>Lentimicrobiaceae</i> fam. nov. Int J Syst Evol Microbiol
66:2635&#x2013;2642. doi: 10.1099/ijsem.0.001103.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1099/ijsem.0.001103</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27098854</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Narihiro T, Terada T, Ohashi A, Kamagata Y, Nakamura K, Sekiguchi Y. 2012. Quantitative detection of previously characterized syntrophic bacteria in anaerobic wastewater treatment systems by sequence-specific rRNA cleavage method. Water Res 46:2167&#x2013;2175. doi: 10.1016/j.watres.2012.01.034.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.watres.2012.01.034</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">22342314</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kuever J.
