owth in the 4 years 2014&#x2013;2017: implications for the Paris agreement. Global Biogeochem Cycles 33:318&#x2013;342. doi: 10.1029/2018GB006009.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1029/2018GB006009</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Yvon-Durocher G, Allen AP, Bastviken D, Conrad R, Gudasz C, St-Pierre A, Thanh-Duc N, del Giorgio PA. 2014. Methane fluxes show consistent temperature dependence across microbial to ecosystem scales. Nature 507:488&#x2013;491. doi: 10.1038/nature13164.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nature13164</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24670769</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Nisbet EG, Dlugokencky EJ, Bousquet P. 2014. Methane on the rise&#x2013;again. Science 343:493&#x2013;495. doi: 10.1126/science.1247828.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1126/science.1247828</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24482471</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Borrel G, J&#xe9;z&#xe9;quel D, Biderre-Petit C, Morel-Desrosiers N, Morel J-P, Peyret P, Fonty G, Lehours A-C. 2011. Production and consumption of methane in freshwater lake ecosystems. Res Microbiol 162:832&#x2013;847. doi: 10.1016/j.resmic.2011.06.004.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.resmic.2011.06.004</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">21704700</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kuivila K, Murray J, Devol A, Lidstrom M, Reimers CE. 1988. Methane cycling in the sediments of Lake Washington. Limnol Oceanogr 33:571&#x2013;581. doi: 10.4319/lo.1988.33.4.0571.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.4319/lo.1988.33.4.0571</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kalyuzhnaya MG, Chistoserdova L. 2005. Community&#x2010;level analysis: genes encoding methanopterin&#x2010;dependent enzymes. Methods Enzymol 397:443&#x2013;454. doi: 10.1016/S0076-6879(05)97027-4.</Citation><ArticleIdLi